        "category": null,
        "deathNote": true,
        "description": {
          "gm": "",
          "value": "<p>When Traseem dies, the Maw's corruption reanimates them into Tras and Eem. Allow the player that slew Traseem to finish their turn. Then, add Tras to the map on the Material Plane, and Eem to the map on the Ethereal Plane. Add Tras to the initiative directly after the player who killed Traseem, and Eem directly after Tras.</p><p>Before Tras's first turn, three players are forcibly sent to the ethereal plane (the first, third, and fifth player in initiative) along with their summons/companions, gaining the Phaselocked - Ethereal Plane effect. The remaining three players are forcibly locked to the Material Plane. Replace the Phaseshift action on their character sheets with Phaselocked Phaseshift.</p><p>On Tras's first turn, they do nothing except prepare to use Kneel Forever on their second turn, gaining the Ready to Reap effect. When this happens, read the following aloud to your players: \"<span style=\"font-family:Roboto, sans-serif\">As Traseem breaks into two, the body remaining on the material plane lifts its scythe in the stance of a farmer ready to cut down wheat</span><span style=\"font-family:'gg sans', 'Noto Sans', 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif\">. The creature is clearly preparing for an incredibly powerful attack.</span><span style=\"font-family:Roboto, sans-serif\">\"</span></p>"
        },
